From 05e22f25fce67e09e9bb29b715005819d5be278a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 14:54:36 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] feat(update): Force update from the backend version pill
 [daveey]

A user-typed turn whose marker has auto_continue=false kept its running tool
call through hermes-sync's core-update drain (not_resumable_reason declined the
pause and the mid-tool cancel), so its admission reservation stayed open and the
apply was "not launchable (admission reservations busy)": in an example incident that
held the gateway update until the turn ended. Right-clicking the backend version pill now
offers "Force update", which pushes the pending update through now.

Core (contract shared with hermes-sync):
- hermes_cli/core_update_force.py: <root>/core-update/force-request
  {"version": 1, "requested_at", "expires_at": requested_at + 1800, "by"},
  written atomically; missing/garbage/expired reads as no request.
  running_turn_count() counts live session_turn_leases rows read-only.
- admission_fence.pause_forced(): the live pause request carries
  "force": true (request_pause(..., force=True) writes it).
- tui_gateway/update_pause.py: under a forced pause a non-resumable turn's
  in-flight calls are cancelled after the same MID_TOOL_GRACE_S and the
  boundary hook ends the turn with FORCED_STOP_REASON. Nothing keeps its
  marker, so it ends like a stopped turn and is not continued (the user
  re-sends it). Pending approvals/clarifies of such a turn are withdrawn with
  a notice saying so. Resumable turns pause and auto-continue as before.
- GET/POST /api/hermes/update/force: available when hermes-sync owes an update
  here (the /api/hermes/update/progress signal), running turn count, pending
  request; POST writes the request (by = token principal or "dashboard"),
  409 when no update is owed.

Desktop:
- StatusbarItem.contextMenuItems: the right-clicked item's actions head the
  bar's existing context menu. The backend pill offers "Force update": GET,
  confirm with the running-turn count, POST, success or error toast; the
  server's message and no confirm when no update can be forced.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
